From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 00:19:55 -0400
Subject: let a Space be given an icon, and be deleted

Spaces could carry an icon since the switcher was built, but nothing could set
one. Right-clicking a Space now offers a short set of icons and a delete.

The set is deliberately small rather than a full emoji picker: the icon only has
to tell one Space from a few others in a row of 24 DIP chips, and a picker would
be a larger surface than the thing it labels.

Delete is disabled on the last Space, matching the model, which already refuses
to remove it -- a window must always have somewhere for its tabs to be.

Why: an icon nobody can set is not a feature.
Removable when: Spaces get a settings surface of their own, where naming and
recolouring belong too.
